# Chaos: effect opacity of my own effects and of the others' (O567, owner 2026-11-14; client/BASE.md "0202"; src/client/chaosfxowner.h
# (new, pure), effect.h/.cpp, missile.h/.cpp, client.h, luafunctions_client.cpp, mods/client_settings/classes/dataset.lua,
# options/effects.otui; after 0001-0201).
# The engine already keeps one alpha per effect source (Client::m_effectAlphas: own, other players, monsters, boss area) and
# Effect / Missile pick one by their source, but the 10.98 server sends no source byte (GameEffectSource off), so the stock draw
# used the "own" alpha for every effect and 0049 left one slider. A hunt where a big earth spell fills the screen with opaque rock
# and dust could not be thinned for the other players' spells without thinning your own.
#  * Source: an Effect or a Missile keeps the source it was marked with; one that was never marked counts as "other" (stock: own).
#    Marks come from the server through the overlay module game_effectopacity (extended opcode 164, client/MANIFEST.md): Lua calls
#    g_client.markEffectSources(source, x, y, z, flat) with {kind, dx, dy, id, ...} (kind 0 effect, 1 missile; at most 400 groups).
#    Each group takes the nearest effect of that id with no source yet on the tile or up to 3 tiles around it (an engine that
#    shifts a big effect, src-patch 0060, sends it a tile or two off the tile a script named), or the best fitting unmarked missile
#    that starts there (the same id first, then the nearest; another id only on the tile or next to it, because src-patch 0045
#    swaps the id of a stock missile). Without marks (an older server, a module that is off) every effect is "other".
#  * Alpha: Effect::draw and Missile::draw use pickSource() and alphaByte(). Effects at 0% are not drawn. A missile's alpha is its
#    source's times Client::m_missileAlpha, the slider "Opacity Missiles" of Options > Effects whose apply called
#    g_client.setMissileAlpha, a function that was never bound (it raised an error), now bound.
#  * Warnings: g_client.setEffectAlphaExempt(id, on) / clearEffectAlphaExempt() name effect ids that always use alpha slot 0 (1.0,
#    never set): the boss warning circles and fills. game_effectopacity hands the list over. Floor telegraphs (game_telegraph) are floor
#    widgets, not effects, and were never touched.
#  * Options > Effects: "Opacity of my effects" (the base key opacityEffects, kept; sets the own alpha) and a new slider "Opacity of
#    other players' effects" (opacityOtherEffects, sets the other alpha), both 0-100% in steps of 5, default 100 (0049 had a floor of
#    25% so warnings never vanished; warnings are exempt now). Each apply tells game_effectopacity (onOption), which asks the server
#    for marks only while the two values differ. The monster and boss alphas stay 1.0: the server cannot tell the engine which
#    effect is a monster's, so monsters' effects follow the "other players" slider.
# Applies after 0001-0201 (the hunks are in files 0049, 0055, 0147, 0152, 0194 and 0199 touch, at lines none of them or 0200 changes).
# Not run in a client; goes live with the next client build.
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/client/chaosfxowner.h
